macpro-fand (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The installed /etc/macpro-fand.conf sets GPU_CAP = {"max": 125}: GPU
    dies at most 125 W by default. The built-in range is unchanged
    (85-200 W); comment the line out for the full range.
  * The budget's reallocation clamps every die to the configured GPU_CAP
    maximum itself (a ceiling below the default share + 10 W could be
    exceeded until the working-temperature ceilings caught up).

 -- Exabit Networks <packages@exabit.io>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 20:42:57 -0000

macpro-fand (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: four zone fan governors with hysteresis, full-speed
    alarms, the 1228 W power budget (CPU first, PL2 held at PL1, uncapped
    devices added to the base load), per-die GPU working-temperature
    ceilings, a load-dependent CPU target, /etc/macpro-fand.conf, and the
    override file for benchmarks.

 -- Exabit Networks <packages@exabit.io>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 14:44:10 +0000
